    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: `sharesHousehold` \u2192 shared `householdId`\n\nThe `sharesHousehold` opt-in already existed (it suppressed the `DuplicateHouseholdException`), but it did not produce a shared household identifier. I added that, keeping each concern in its natural place:\n\n**1. Stable ID derivation \u2014 `util/HouseholdIdGenerator.java` (new)**\nA small, single-purpose utility that derives the household identifier as a deterministic SHA-256 digest of the normalized `lastName` + `address` pair (reusing the existing `TextNormalizer`). Because it's deterministic, every member of a household computes the same value and it never drifts \u2014 i.e. genuinely \"stable and shared.\"\n\n**2. Persistence of the join \u2014 `ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`**\nAdded `joinHousehold(owner, existingMembers)`: it stamps the new owner with the household ID and back-fills any existing member that doesn't yet carry it (persisting only those that changed), returning the ID. This lives in the service/transactional layer where repository writes belong.\n\n**3. Orchestration \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`**\nRefactored so the household lookup runs once; when `sharesHousehold` is true it delegates to `joinHousehold` before saving, otherwise it still throws `DuplicateHouseholdException` on a conflict. No duplicated logic.\n\n**4. Model & wire format**\n- `Owner` gains a `householdId` field mapped to a new `household_id` column.\n- `household_id` added to all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n- `householdId` added as a read-only property on the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, so the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct mapper expose it automatically \u2014 that's how `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` (joiners `b` and `c` receive the same non-blank `householdId`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
